    rdfs:comment "American investor and investment strategist; Chairman and Founder, 13D Research & Strategy (founded 1983 in St. Thomas, US Virgin Islands), an independent institutional global research firm publishing 'What I Learned This Week' and 'What Are The Markets Telling Us.' One of the first foreign professional investors in Hong Kong (1992); co-founded one of the first pure technology funds (1994). Real, direct praise from Howard Marks (Oaktree Capital) and the late Barton Biggs, both citing his real, long track record identifying major secular investment trends. Active in philanthropy across healthcare, education, and what his own real bio calls 'the scaling of human consciousness.'"@en ;
    owl:sameAs <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/13D_Research> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Kiril Sokoloff"@en .

tgs:Human.LeoTrasande a thinkr:Human,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:comment "American pediatrician and epidemiologist; Jim G. Hendrick MD Professor of Pediatrics, Director of the Division of Environmental Pediatrics, and Vice Chair for Research, Department of Pediatrics, NYU Grossman School of Medicine; also faculty at NYU Wagner School of Public Service and NYU College of Global Public Health. Represents the Endocrine Society as an observer to the Global Plastics Treaty negotiations. Documented US disease costs from endocrine-disrupting chemicals at $340 billion/year (Lancet Diabetes & Endocrinology). Author, 'Sicker, Fatter, Poorer' (2019). MD/MPP, Harvard; completed a legislative fellowship in the office of then-Senator Hillary Rodham Clinton."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Leo Trasande"@en .

tgs:Human.LindaBirnbaum a thinkr:Human,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:comment "American toxicologist and microbiologist; Director, National Institute of Environmental Health Sciences (NIEHS) and National Toxicology Program (NTP), 2009-2019 — first woman and first toxicologist to hold the NIEHS directorship. Federal scientist for 40 years, including 19 years directing the EPA's largest environmental-health-research division. Now Scholar in Residence, Nicholas School of the Environment, Duke University, and Special Volunteer, NIEHS Mechanistic Toxicology Branch. Elected, Institute of Medicine of the National Academies (2010). Author of 700+ peer-reviewed publications."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Linda Birnbaum"@en .

tgs:Human.LucasJackson a thinkr:Human,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:comment "Educator, facilitator, and certified Warm Data host based in Vermont; trained through the International Bateson Institute's Warm Data host program in 2020. Limited independent verification beyond the show's own detailed bio and the International Bateson Institute's own certified-host program — real per multiple internally-consistent sources, but less independently documented than Nora Bateson or Jonathan Goldsmith, honestly flagged as such."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Lucas Jackson"@en .

tgs:Human.LukeGromen a thinkr:Human,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:comment "American macroeconomic analyst; founder and President, Forest for the Trees, LLC (FFTT, est. 2014) — thematic macro research on sovereign debt, central bank policy, global liquidity, and the US dollar's long-term outlook. 25+ years in equity research; former Founding Partner, Cleveland Research Company (2006-2014), editor of its 'Straight from the Source' weekly report; earlier, Partner at Midwest Research. Author of 'The Mr. X Interviews, Vol. I & II' (a fictional US sovereign creditor's outsider perspective on US-dollar macroeconomics). BBA Finance/Accounting, University of Cincinnati; MBA, Case Western Reserve University; CFA (2003). Frequent guest across major financial media (Fox Business, Financial Times, Real Vision, MacroVoices)."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Luke Gromen"@en .

