    rdfs:comment "American lawyer and policy consultant, 30+ years in policy, law, finance, and strategic communications. Special Assistant to President Clinton and Senior Director for Russian, Ukrainian and Eurasian Affairs, National Security Council (2000-2001); Deputy Assistant Secretary of the Treasury for International Affairs under Robert Rubin and Lawrence Summers (1997-2000). Vice Chair, Panterra (London strategic consultancy); co-founder, Keep Our Republic (democratic-governance nonprofit); life member, Council on Foreign Relations. Educated Harvard, Oxford (Merton College), Georgetown. No independent Wikipedia/DBpedia page found — confirmed real via Carnegie Endowment, Georgetown ISD, and multiple other independent professional listings."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Mark Medish"@en .

