tgs:Human.MichaelEvery a thinkr:Human,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:comment "Global Strategist, Rabobank Singapore, analyzing geopolitics/economics/markets intersections. 25+ years as economist/strategist across roles at Silk Road Associates (Bangkok), Royal Bank of Canada (London/Sydney), and Dun & Bradstreet (London); has lived and worked in 9-10 countries. Invited presenter, 2022 G-20. BA, Lancaster University; master's, University College London. Real, extensive prior TGS history confirmed: Reality Roundtable #16, Reality Roundtable #12, and Episode #118 ('The Many-Isms of the Metacrisis') — none built as Episode individuals in this pass. No independent Wikipedia/DBpedia page found — confirmed real via Rabobank's own staff page and extensive independent financial-media coverage."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Michael Every"@en .

tgs:Human.MikeJoy a thinkr:Human,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:comment "New Zealand freshwater ecologist and science communicator (b. 1959); Senior Researcher, Institute for Governance and Policy Studies, Victoria University of Wellington (formerly Massey University). 20+ years publicly advocating for New Zealand freshwater-quality reform, especially against nutrient pollution from intensive dairying — drew criticism from the dairy industry and a former Prime Minister. Left school at 17, worked as a truck driver, farmhand, and NZ Security Intelligence Service agent before enrolling at Massey University at 33. Author of the memoir 'The Fight for Freshwater.' Recipient, Universities NZ inaugural Critic and Conscience of Society Award; Charles Fleming Award for Environmental Achievement (2013); Forest & Bird's Old Blue Award (2011)."@en ;
    owl:sameAs <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mike_Joy_(freshwater_ecologist)> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Mike Joy"@en .

tgs:Human.MohitTrivedi a thinkr:Human,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:comment "Indian learning designer, facilitator, and movement weaver; co-founder and Steward, 2069 Ecosystem (a collective committed to a 50-year vision responding to the metacrisis, alongside Abhishek Thakore). Founder, Mukt-Dhara Open Learning Space. Background in psychology, nursing, alternative education, and social entrepreneurship. Lives in Udaipur, South Rajasthan, as part of an unschooling family."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Mohit Trivedi"@en .

tgs:Human.NancyMcWilliams a thinkr:Human,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:comment "Psychoanalyst and personality theorist. Professor Emerita, Graduate School of Applied and Professional Psychology, Rutgers University. Author of 'Psychoanalytic Diagnosis' (a standard training text) and Associate Editor of the Psychodynamic Diagnostic Manual (PDM). Past president, Division of Psychoanalysis (39), American Psychological Association."@en ;
    owl:sameAs <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Nancy_McWilliams> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Nancy McWilliams"@en .

tgs:Human.NatashaLinhart a thinkr:Human,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:comment "BSc, Politics, Psychology, Law and Economics (focus: Economics and Business; electives in Degrowth and Critical Theory), University of Amsterdam, 2023. Founder, IBCompanions (high-school tutoring company). Real, direct, ongoing professional relationship: Research Associate / Program Associate, the Institute for the Study of Energy and Our Future (ISEOF) — Nate Hagens' own organization — confirmed independently via ISEOF's own management team listing."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Natasha Linhart"@en .

tgs:Human.NoraBateson a thinkr:Human,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:comment "Filmmaker, writer, researcher, and educator; founder and president of the International Bateson Institute. Daughter of systems thinker Gregory Bateson (already tgs:Human.GregoryBateson in this graph). Author of 'Small Arcs of Larger Circles' (Triarchy Press, 2016), 'Combining' (Triarchy Press, 2023 — CORRECTED 2026-08-13 from an earlier, wrong 2024 date), and 'Belly' (Triarchy Press, 2026); director of the documentary 'An Ecology of Mind' (2010), a portrait of her father. Coined 'Warm Data' (~2012), 'Symmathesy' (2015, presented at ISSS), and (per her own LinkedIn bio) 'Aphanipoiesis' and 'Ready-ing' too."@en ;
    owl:sameAs <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Nora_Bateson> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Nora Bateson"@en .

tgs:Human.PedroPrieto a thinkr:Human,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:comment "Telecom engineer (30 years, ITT R&D Labs and Alcatel) turned solar-energy analyst. Vice president and co-founder of AEREN (Asociación para el Estudio de los Recursos Energéticos), which represents ASPO (Association for the Study of Peak Oil and Gas) in Spain; board member of ASPO International. Led several real solar PV installations in Spain since 2004. Co-author with Charles A. S. Hall (a real, notable EROI researcher and Odum student already referenced elsewhere in this graph via Concept.MaximumPowerPrinciple) of 'Spain's Photovoltaic Revolution: The Energy Return on Investment' (2013) — the first complete real-world EROI energy analysis of a large-scale PV deployment, finding real EROI too low to seamlessly support an energy transition."@en ;
    owl:sameAs <https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pedro_Prieto> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Pedro Prieto"@en .

tgs:Human.PellaThiel a thinkr:Human,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:comment "Swedish ecologist, part-time farmer, and educator in ecopsychology; MSc Ecology, Stockholm University (thesis on Ecuadorian rainforest restoration). Co-founder, Swedish Transition Network and End Ecocide Sweden (current chairperson); knowledge expert, UN Harmony with Nature programme. Recipient, Swedish Martin Luther King Award (2023) and Environmental Hero of the Year (2019). Real later solo TGS appearance confirmed: Episode #121 ('Criminalizing Ecocide: The Rights of Nature'), which itself directly cross-references this RR-5 appearance."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Pella Thiel"@en .

tgs:Human.PeterKilde a thinkr:Human,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:comment "American anti-poverty and affordable-housing administrator; Executive Director, West CAP (West Central Wisconsin Community Action Agency), 1995-2024. Chaired the National Community Action Partnership's 'New Reality Initiative' on how peak oil, resource depletion, and economic turmoil affect low-income communities; board member, Association for the Study of Peak Oil & Gas USA (ASPO-USA) — a real, direct professional grounding in Nate's own core subject matter predating this podcast. Recipient, 2013 Charles M. Hill Sr. Award for Housing Excellence. Lives on a small farm near Spring Valley, Wisconsin."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Peter Kilde"@en .

tgs:Human.PeterWard a thinkr:Human,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:comment "American paleontologist and astrobiologist; Professor of Biology and of Earth and Space Sciences, University of Washington; former Principal Investigator, UW node of the NASA Astrobiology Institute (2001-2006). Co-originator of the Rare Earth Hypothesis (with Donald Brownlee); originator of the Medea Hypothesis (2009 book) — the argument, opposing James Lovelock's Gaia Hypothesis, that life on Earth has repeatedly driven its own mass extinctions via self-destructive biochemical feedbacks (ocean anoxia, hydrogen sulfide release). Author of 17+ books including 'Under a Green Sky' and 'On Methuselah's Trail.' Real prior TGS solo appearance confirmed: Episode #8."@en ;
    owl:sameAs <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Peter_Ward_(paleontologist)> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Peter Ward"@en .

tgs:Human.PriscillaTrinh a thinkr:Human,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:comment "American communicator and food-systems activist; Director of Communications, Post Growth Institute; co-coordinator, Minnesota Youth Institute; creator, #postgrowth jobs board; founding member, The Overstory Alliance (co-founded Movement School and coordinated the Line 3 pipeline-resistance media collective). Editor, Blue Marble Review; contributor, Minnesota Women's Press. BS, Sustainable Systems Management, University of Minnesota-Twin Cities; 2019 Borlaug-Ruan intern, International Rice Research Institute (Philippines). Real, direct, multi-year prior relationship with Nate Hagens: was his student and teaching assistant for his University of Minnesota class 'Reality 101,' known to him since age 17."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Priscilla Trịnh"@en .

tgs:Human.RachelCarson a thinkr:Human,
