    owl:sameAs <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Scott_Barry_Kaufman> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Scott Barry Kaufman"@en .

tgs:Human.ShannaSwan a thinkr:Human,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:comment "Environmental and reproductive epidemiologist; Professor of Environmental Medicine and Public Health, Icahn School of Medicine at Mount Sinai (NYC); Director, Action Science Initiative. Published 200+ scientific papers on environmental chemical exposure and reproductive/neurodevelopmental effects. Co-author, 'Countdown: How Our Modern World Is Threatening Sperm Counts...' (2021). Central figure in the 2026 Netflix documentary 'The Plastic Detox,' running a real 3-month endocrine-disrupting-chemical-reduction intervention with 6 couples facing unexplained infertility. Real prior TGS solo appearance confirmed: Episode #2 ('Sperm and Our Future') — one of the first-ever guests on the podcast."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Shanna Swan"@en .

tgs:Human.SianSutherland a thinkr:Human,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:comment "British entrepreneur; co-founder, A Plastic Planet (2017, with Frederikke Magnussen) — created the world's first plastic-free supermarket aisle (Amsterdam, 2018); co-founder, PlasticFree (materials/systems solutions platform) and the Plastic Free Babies campaign. Previously ran a Michelin-starred restaurant and a beauty/skincare brand-design agency. At the 2023 UN Plastics Treaty negotiations (INC2), launched the Plastic Health Council with Plastic Soup Foundation. Real prior TGS solo appearance confirmed: Episode #89 ('Innovating the Business of Plastics')."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Sian Sutherland"@en .

tgs:Human.SigmundFreud a thinkr:Human,
