    owl:sameAs <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Sigmund_Freud> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Sigmund Freud"@en .

tgs:Human.SimonMichaux a thinkr:Human,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:comment "Associate Professor of Geometallurgy, Geological Survey of Finland (GTK), Circular Economy Solutions Unit. PhD in Mining Engineering (JKMRC, University of Queensland). 18 years in the Australian mining industry before moving to Belgium (University of Liège) and then Finland to research industrial recycling and the circular economy. Author of the widely-cited 2021 GTK report 'Restructuring the Circular Economy into the Resource Balanced Economy,' arguing existing green-transition mineral-supply plans are logistically impractical at proposed scale. No independent Wikipedia/DBpedia page found — confirmed real via GTK's own staff page, Google Scholar (897+ citations), and his own site."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Simon Michaux"@en .

tgs:Human.SkyeCielitaFlor a thinkr:Human,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:comment "South African-born folk herbalist, grief ritualist, and plant-medicine practitioner, based in Australia; early years in wildlife rehabilitation and as a wilderness guide in the South African bush. Completed a 3-year traditional Taoist healing apprenticeship, then a full-time 5-year traditional curanderismo apprenticeship (2011-2016) with Shipibo teachers of the Mahua-Lopez lineage in the Peruvian Amazon. Facilitator of Experiential Deep Ecology and the Work That Reconnects; co-facilitator, 'The Mythic Body' (year-long course by Josh Schrei); incorporates Francis Weller's Five Gates of Grief framework into her own grief-ritual facilitation."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Skye Cielita Flor"@en .

tgs:Human.SkyeNeville a thinkr:Human,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:comment "Young environmental activist from near Fairbourne, North Wales — a village publicly described as at risk of being among the first climate-driven relocations in the Western world. Campaigns against single-use plastic wrap on children's comics and magazines (multi-year campaign, described in this episode as having recently achieved industry-wide roundtable engagement across UK distributors, manufacturers, supermarkets, and retailers). Featured in Damon Gameau's documentary 'Future Council' (2024). Enthusiastic sailor."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Skye Neville"@en .

tgs:Human.SteffiBednarek a thinkr:Human,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:comment "Gestalt psychotherapist, trauma therapist, and climate psychologist (25+ years, systemic change and trauma therapy); founder and director, Centre for Climate Psychology. Editor of 'Climate, Psychology, and Change' (contributors include Bayo Akomolafe, Nora Bateson, Thomas Hübl, and Francis Weller — both Bateson and Weller already real, built figures in this graph). Has worked with national governments, corporate/financial institutions, and NGOs on the psychological dimension of climate decision-making; creator of the 'Systems Wayfinding' initiative applying IFS to organizations and institutions. Associate member, American Psychological Association's climate change group."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Steffi Bednarek"@en .

tgs:Human.StephanieHoopes a thinkr:Human,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:comment "American researcher; National Director, United For ALICE (United Way of Northern New Jersey). Developed the ALICE (Asset Limited, Income Constrained, Employed) measure as a 2009 pilot study of Morris County, NJ while an Assistant Professor at Rutgers University-Newark's School of Public Affairs and Administration (2011-2015); has since expanded ALICE to cover all ~3,000 US counties. PhD, London School of Economics; MA, UNC Chapel Hill; BA, Wellesley College. Formerly taught at Rutgers-Newark, Columbia, and the Universities of Sussex and Birmingham (UK)."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Stephanie Hoopes"@en .

tgs:Human.SteveKeen a thinkr:Human,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:comment "Australian heterodox economist (b. Mar 28, 1953); Honorary/Distinguished Research Fellow, University College London; formerly Professor, Kingston University London and University of Western Sydney. Author of 'Debunking Economics' and 'The New Economics: A Manifesto.' One of a small number of economists who publicly anticipated the 2008 Global Financial Crisis in advance (Revere Award, Real World Economics Review). Creator of the open-source system dynamics modeling software Minsky."@en ;
    owl:sameAs <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Steve_Keen> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Steve Keen"@en .

tgs:Human.TheoDawson a thinkr:Human,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:comment "American developmental psychologist; founder and Executive Director, Lectica, Inc. (nonprofit developing evidence-based developmental assessments); creator of the Computerized Lectical Assessment System (CLAS) and the MindLog educational tool. PhD, Graduate School of Education, UC Berkeley (1998, dissertation on measuring learning pathways). Former positions include Director, Developmental Assessment Project (UC Berkeley) and instructor, Harvard Graduate School of Education. Real, direct prior academic collaborator of tgs:Persona.ZakStein — co-published 'Epistemological development: It's all relative' (2004, Jean Piaget Society) before either appeared on this podcast; Stein was her doctoral-era research collaborator and is co-founder of Lectica."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Theo Dawson"@en .

tgs:Human.TomMurphy a thinkr:Human,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:comment "Professor Emeritus of Physics and Astronomy & Astrophysics, UC San Diego. Led the APOLLO (Apache Point Observatory Lunar Laser-ranging Operation) project testing General Relativity via reflectors left on the Moon by Apollo astronauts. Author of 'Energy and Human Ambitions on a Finite Planet' (2021, UC open-access textbook) and a 2022 Nature Physics paper arguing physical resource exhaustion precedes waste-heat limits in constraining GDP growth. Writes the 'Do the Math' blog since 2011."@en ;
    owl:sameAs <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Tom_Murphy_(physicist)> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Tom Murphy"@en .

tgs:Human.UgoBardi a thinkr:Human,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    owl:sameAs <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Ugo_Bardi> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Ugo Bardi"@en .

tgs:Human.VandanaShiva a thinkr:Human,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:comment "Indian scientist, environmental activist, ecofeminist, and author; PhD in Theoretical Physics (quantum theory, hidden variables/non-locality), University of Western Ontario. Founder, Research Foundation for Science, Technology and Ecology (1982) and Navdanya ('nine seeds,' 1991) — biodiversity/seed-sovereignty movement now serving 500,000+ farmers across 16 Indian states. Early volunteer with the Chipko movement. Recipient, Right Livelihood Award (1993) and Sydney Peace Prize. Author of 20+ books including 'The Violence of the Green Revolution' and 'Monocultures of the Mind.'"@en ;
    owl:sameAs <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Vandana_Shiva> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Vandana Shiva"@en .

tgs:Human.WendellBerry a thinkr:Human,
