    skos:prefLabel "William R. Catton Jr."@en .

tgs:Human.WilliamRees a thinkr:Human,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:comment "Canadian ecologist, ecological economist, Professor Emeritus, School of Community and Regional Planning, University of British Columbia (b. Dec 18, 1943). Originator and co-developer (with then-PhD-student Mathis Wackernagel) of Ecological Footprint Analysis, introduced in their 1996 book 'Our Ecological Footprint,' now translated into 8+ languages and among the world's best-known sustainability metrics. Fellow, Royal Society of Canada (2006); Trudeau Foundation Fellow (2007); 2012 Blue Planet Prize (jointly with Wackernagel)."@en ;
    owl:sameAs <http://dbpedia.org/resource/William_E._Rees> ;
    skos:prefLabel "William E. Rees"@en .

tgs:Human.WilliamStanleyJevons a thinkr:Human,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    owl:sameAs <http://dbpedia.org/resource/William_Stanley_Jevons> ;
    skos:prefLabel "William Stanley Jevons"@en .

tgs:Human.ZachWeiss a thinkr:Human,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:comment "American watershed-restoration practitioner; founder, Elemental Ecosystems (ecological development/water-retention landscape design, 25+ countries across 6 continents) and Water Stories (educational platform/community, founded ~2021 after a formative 2019 meeting with Indian water activist Rajendra Singh). First person to earn the Holzer Practitioner certification directly from Austrian farmer Sepp Holzer, via a 2-year apprenticeship. Focuses on decentralized water retention and the 'biotic pump' mechanism — living ecosystems drawing atmospheric moisture inland from oceans — as central to climate regulation."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Zach Weiss"@en .

tgs:Human.ZakStein a thinkr:Human,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:comment "Philosopher of education (EdD, Harvard). Co-founder of Lectica, Inc. (research-based reform of large-scale standardized testing, co-founded as a Harvard student), Civilization Research Institute, the Consilience Project, and the Center for World Philosophy and Religion. Author of 'Education in a Time Between Worlds' and other works. Real, direct professional connection to tgs:Persona.DanielSchmachtenberger (both on the scientific advisory board of Neurohacker Collective, per independent verification) — not modeled as a formal Relationship in this pass, noted here only. No independent Wikipedia/DBpedia page found — confirmed real via his own site (zakstein.org) and multiple independent, mutually-consistent professional/podcast sources."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Zak Stein"@en .

