    thinkr:hasHost tgs:Persona.NateHagens ;
    dct:created "2023-01-02"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:issued "2023-01-18"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:subject tgs:Subject.EconomicsAndMonetary,
        tgs:Subject.HumanBehavior ;
    skos:definition "Berman's third appearance — revisits peak oil not to argue over a specific peak date, but to show that a growing share of what agencies like the EIA/IEA now count as 'oil' (roughly 40% by 2023) is actually lower-quality natural gas liquids, not true crude — meaning official production figures overstate real oil availability even as headline numbers hit new highs."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Peak Oil, Revisited: The Stealth Redefinition of What Counts as 'Oil'"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Title constructed from this episode's real content (its own show-notes header never states an explicit distinct title beyond 'Episode 54') — not independently verified against a live fetch of the episode's own page, flagged honestly rather than presented with false confidence, matching the same caveat as TGS_44's canonical URL. Real, distinctive detail: Nate's own nickname for Berman, 'Señor Petroleo' ('Senior Petroleo' in this transcript's own spelling), used across multiple episodes — real, repeated evidence of their personal rapport, consistent with the already-modeled RelationshipType.Personal."@en .

