tgs:Scenario.GS-CI-FN-SW a thinkr:Scenario,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    thinkr:hasAlternateTerm [ a thinkr:AlternateTerm ;
            thinkr:hasAlternateTermType tgs:AlternateTermType.ExactMatch ;
            skos:prefLabel "The Long Repair"@en ;
            skos:scopeNote "RENAMED 2026-08-13 from tgs:Scenario.TheLongRepair to the systematic position-code IRI, per MJSullivan's explicit direction (matching the EnergyReturnOnInvestment precedent — canonical form is the systematic one, human name demoted to AlternateTerm). No dangling references existed before the rename (confirmed via grep across the whole data/seed/ directory)." ] ;
    thinkr:hasEarthSystemsXPosition 2 ;
    thinkr:hasEarthSystemsYPosition 4 ;
    thinkr:hasEconomicXPosition 2 ;
    thinkr:hasEconomicYPosition 4 ;
    thinkr:hasFacet tgs:ScenarioFacet.CivicIdeal,
        tgs:ScenarioFacet.FriendlyNeighborsWithGoodFences,
        tgs:ScenarioFacet.StrainedButWorkable,
        tgs:ScenarioFacet.TheGreatSimplification ;
    thinkr:hasGeopoliticalXPosition 2 ;
    thinkr:hasGeopoliticalYPosition 4 ;
    thinkr:hasPowerAndDistributionXPosition 2 ;
    thinkr:hasPowerAndDistributionYPosition 4 ;
    dct:source <https://www.thegreatsimplification.com> ;
    skos:definition "Managed contraction combined with broadly shared power, cooperative regionally-self-sufficient geopolitics, and a strained-but-still-functional biosphere. Explicitly named by Hagens as the aspirational path — hard to reach and, in his own framing, the hardest of the 4 to hold once reached (since it depends entirely on maintaining trust and legitimacy while material throughput is falling), but the one he considers most worth striving toward. He notes it will read as failure/decline by every conventional growth-based metric even while representing genuine improvement in lived experience — a healing-vs-dying confusion he considers one of the deepest challenges in the whole framework."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Great Simplification + Civic Ideal + Friendly Neighbors + Strained But Workable"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "RENAMED 2026-08-13 (second rename) from tgs:Scenario.A-E-I-M to a 2-letter mnemonic code, per MJSullivan's explicit request — more readable than an arbitrary single-letter position. prefLabel changed from the bare code to a spelled-out concatenation of its 4 real component Facet names. NOTE, same tradeoff class as this Scenario's own denormalized X/Y positions: this prefLabel is DERIVED FROM (and must stay in sync with) its component Facets' own prefLabels via hasFacet — if a Facet's own name ever changes, this label can silently go stale unless updated to match. Confirmed via grep this rename required updating references in episodes.ttl too (unlike the original TheLongRepair->A-E-I-M rename, which had zero external references at the time)."@en .

tgs:Scenario.GS-FF-CW-HT a thinkr:Scenario,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    thinkr:hasAlternateTerm [ a thinkr:AlternateTerm ;
            thinkr:hasAlternateTermType tgs:AlternateTermType.ExactMatch ;
            skos:prefLabel "Fortress World"@en ;
            skos:scopeNote "RENAMED 2026-08-13 from tgs:Scenario.FortressWorld to the systematic position-code IRI, per MJSullivan's explicit direction (matching the EnergyReturnOnInvestment precedent — canonical form is the systematic one, human name demoted to AlternateTerm). No dangling references existed before the rename (confirmed via grep across the whole data/seed/ directory)." ] ;
    thinkr:hasEarthSystemsXPosition 2 ;
    thinkr:hasEarthSystemsYPosition 2 ;
    thinkr:hasEconomicXPosition 2 ;
    thinkr:hasEconomicYPosition 4 ;
    thinkr:hasFacet tgs:ScenarioFacet.ForcedFeudalism,
        tgs:ScenarioFacet.HothouseTriage,
        tgs:ScenarioFacet.TheColdWarScenario,
        tgs:ScenarioFacet.TheGreatSimplification ;
    thinkr:hasGeopoliticalXPosition 2 ;
    thinkr:hasGeopoliticalYPosition 2 ;
    thinkr:hasPowerAndDistributionXPosition 4 ;
    thinkr:hasPowerAndDistributionYPosition 2 ;
    dct:source <https://www.thegreatsimplification.com> ;
    skos:definition "What happens when real economic contraction arrives and those in power choose to hoard rather than share it. Hagens describes daily life here as tightly controlled but not necessarily chaotic — a grim, known order (his own comparison: The Hunger Games) where some people and regions are actively written off to protect others. He argues it's fragile over the long run because active control/surveillance is itself energy- and complexity-intensive, which becomes progressively harder to sustain as the underlying resource base contracts."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Great Simplification + Forced Feudalism + Cold War Scenario + Hothouse Triage"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "RENAMED 2026-08-13 (second rename) from tgs:Scenario.A-H-K-O to a 2-letter mnemonic code, per MJSullivan's explicit request — more readable than an arbitrary single-letter position. prefLabel changed from the bare code to a spelled-out concatenation of its 4 real component Facet names. NOTE, same tradeoff class as this Scenario's own denormalized X/Y positions: this prefLabel is DERIVED FROM (and must stay in sync with) its component Facets' own prefLabels via hasFacet — if a Facet's own name ever changes, this label can silently go stale unless updated to match. Confirmed via grep this rename required updating references in episodes.ttl too (unlike the original TheLongRepair->A-E-I-M rename, which had zero external references at the time)."@en .

tgs:Scenario.MM-FF-CW-CB a thinkr:Scenario,
