thinkr:ReliabilityType a thinkr:Category,
        owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Enumerated reliability of a thinkr:Source (the publication/venue), independent of what any given piece of evidence from it argues. A source's tier is an editorial judgment call, not an objective formula — expect it to need periodic revisiting, the same way Wikipedia's own reliable-sources list is a living, contested, human-adjudicated thing."@en ;
    owl:equivalentClass [ a owl:Class ;
            owl:oneOf ( thinkr:ReliabilityType.Authoritative thinkr:ReliabilityType.Reputable thinkr:ReliabilityType.Unverified thinkr:ReliabilityType.Unreliable ) ] ;
    skos:prefLabel "Reliability Type"@en .

thinkr:ResponsePhase a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "One of the 3 overlapping timeline phases from Frankly_132's action framework — Phase A (the Stability Window), Phase B (Bend Not Break), Phase C (the Stable Attractor). Explicitly NOT sequential in the sense of complete-and-move-on: Hagens frames all 3 as genuinely overlapping and path-dependent, with Phase C reachable only by building through A and B, not by skipping them. Each of the 6 InterventionFronts has real, distinct work appropriate to each Phase, per Hagens' own framing, though the episode itself doesn't enumerate that cross-product in detail for all 30 Subdomains — not fabricated here where the primary source doesn't specify it."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Response Phase"@en .

