    thinkr:hasYPosition 1 ;
    thinkr:relatesTo tgs:Concept.GreatSimplification ;
    thinkr:xAxisDivergentFrom tgs:ScenarioFacet.MadMax ;
    thinkr:yAxisDivergentFrom tgs:ScenarioFacet.GreenGrowth ;
    skos:definition "Economic contraction combined with coordination and real ecological stewardship — Hagens' own real, direct phrasing from Frankly_139."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "The Great Simplification"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "SPLIT 2026-08-13 from tgs:Concept.GreatSimplification, which was dual-typed as both Concept and ScenarioFacet — reversing that consolidation, itself a reversal of an even earlier attempt at exactly this same split (see tgs:Concept.GreatSimplification's own scopeNote for that history). MJSullivan's own reasoning: a Concept and a ScenarioFacet genuinely have different attributes (general prose definition vs. grid-positional data) and different real usage patterns confirmed via a full audit of every triple involving the old dual-typed individual — hasFacet (from tgs:Scenario.GS-CI-FN-SW and tgs:Scenario.GS-FF-CW-HT) and favorsFacet (from tgs:SchoolOfThought.DegrowthMovement) require the grid-specific role by their own property definitions and now point here; discusses/dct:references/contrastsWith were all genuinely about the general umbrella idea and stayed on the Concept. thinkr:relatesTo used as the explicit link between the two split individuals — the safe general choice, not a newly-invented specific property; worth reconsidering if more Concept/ScenarioFacet splits happen later and a pattern emerges. Position ALSO CORRECTED 2026-08-13, same day, from (X=2,Y=4) to (X=2,Y=2) — see tgs:ScenarioDimension.Economic's own scopeNote for the full correction (real chart PDF supplied by MJSullivan). Real-world meaning unchanged (Contracting + within ecological limits); only the axis-letter assignment was wrong."@en .

thinkr:AlternateTermType a thinkr:Category,
        owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "The TYPE of relationship an AlternateTerm has to its parent Concept — genuinely interchangeable (ExactMatch), close but not identical (CloseMatch), broader/narrower in a hierarchical sense (BroadMatch/NarrowMatch), a loose non-hierarchical association (Related), an opposing idea (Antonym), or a shortened lexical form of the same term (Abbreviation). This typing is the whole point of this mechanism over a bare skos:altLabel string — it's what lets a future discovery UI distinguish 'search for this and get the exact same thing' from 'search for this and get pointed somewhere adjacent.' NOTE (added 2026-08-13): Abbreviation is a genuinely DIFFERENT AXIS from the other 5 — it describes LEXICAL FORM (is this a shortened spelling), not semantic distance. An abbreviation is by definition ALSO an ExactMatch semantically (same meaning, different surface form) — thinkr:hasAlternateTermType has no cardinality restriction specifically so BOTH can be asserted on the same AlternateTerm when both are true, rather than forcing a choice between them."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Alternate Term Type"@en .

thinkr:InterventionFront a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "One of Hagens' 6 broad fronts of intervention from Frankly_132's 'first public draft' action framework — Infrastructure & Physical Stock/Flow, Poverty & Displacement, Ecological Interventions, Civic Resilience & Governance, Culture & Meaning, and Economic Transition. Explicitly framed by Hagens as interdependent, not a menu to pick from, and each operating at multiple real scales (community/local, regional, national, global)."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Intervention Front"@en .

thinkr:ProfessionalRole a thinkr:Category,
        owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "A person's intrinsic professional identity (Educator, Author, etc.) — deliberately generic and reusable across any future thinker's graph, same reasoning as thinkr:EpisodeType. Distinct from thinkr:PersonEntityType, which describes a person's RELATIONSHIP TO THIS SPECIFIC PROJECT (Guest, Contributor), not something intrinsic to them independent of it. GAP FOUND AND FLAGGED 2026-08-13, raised by MJSullivan: this class and its property (thinkr:hasProfessionalRole) existed since early in the project but had only ever actually been populated via the narrower thinkr:hasTGSRole sub-property, applied only to tgs:Persona.NateHagens himself — zero of the 70+ other real Personas built this session had ever received a thinkr:hasProfessionalRole assertion, despite the general mechanism being ready to use. Politician, Environmentalist, and Physicist added this same day as real, immediately-needed values (Richard Gephardt, tgs:Persona.RichardGephardt, is the first non-Nate Persona to receive a thinkr:hasProfessionalRole assertion). Retroactively auditing and tagging the other 70+ existing Personas is a separate, much larger task — NOT done in this pass, worth treating as its own deliberate effort rather than folding in silently."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Professional Role"@en .

tgs:Concept.DistributedAgency a thinkr:Concept,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dct:subject tgs:Subject.HumanBehavior ;
    skos:definition "A real, recurring pattern across independently-recorded episodes: meaningful change comes from ordinary, distributed action rather than a singular hero or savior figure. Direct textual evidence spans multiple episodes, not one coined term: Frankly_58's own real closing reframe (Sam and Gollum, not Frodo, as the actual Catalysts who changed Lord of the Rings' outcome — 'you never know when your actions could shift the larger story'); Frankly_132's direct claim that reluctance to lead 'might be a good indication that you could be a good leader tomorrow,' paired with its critique that modern systems select for Dark Triad traits in those who actively seek leadership; RR-17's two guests independently converging on 'find like-minded people close to home' as their practical closing advice, rather than pointing toward a movement or a leader; and the real, structural logic of Buckminster Fuller's trim-tab principle (small, precisely-placed, unglamorous leverage redirecting something enormous), which is also the real source of Priscilla Trịnh's own 'Trintab' nickname from RR-9."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Distributed Agency, Not Saviors"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Identified and named as a real pattern by MJSullivan during this session, not something Hagens has explicitly unified under one term himself — worth being honest about that distinction even though the pattern itself is real and evidence-grounded across genuinely independent sources."@en .

tgs:Concept.GreatSimplification a thinkr:Concept,
        thinkr:HagensConcept,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    thinkr:contrastsWith tgs:SchoolOfThought.TechnoOptimism ;
    thinkr:relatesTo tgs:ScenarioFacet.TheGreatSimplification ;
    dct:source <https://www.thegreatsimplification.com> ;
    dct:subject tgs:Subject.SystemsFrameworks ;
    skos:definition "Hagens' term for a coming, likely non-linear reduction in the complexity, energy throughput, and material consumption of global civilization, as fossil fuel surplus energy declines relative to what the economy has grown to expect."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "The Great Simplification"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "contrastsWith added 2026-08-13. Real, direct evidence, not inferred from tone alone: RR-24's own official episode description centers its entire premise on critiquing techno-optimists' space-colonization ambitions as a way of 'bypassing the problems we now face on Earth' — this graph's own already-built Concept.EnergyBlindness makes the same underlying critique in general form. MJSullivan's own framing, worth preserving: this graph's discipline is about verifying real sources, not about false neutrality — Hagens' own real material already takes a clear, evidenced side here. SPLIT 2026-08-13: this individual was dual-typed as both Concept and ScenarioFacet (added, then reverted from an even earlier split attempt, then re-split here) — now holds the Concept role only, with the grid-specific ScenarioFacet role split out to its own individual, tgs:ScenarioFacet.TheGreatSimplification, linked via thinkr:relatesTo. See that individual's own scopeNote for the full reasoning and migration record."@en .

tgs:DoughnutHalf.EcologicalCeiling a thinkr:DoughnutHalf,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dct:source tgs:Work.CaliforniaDoughnutReport2025 ;
    skos:definition "The outer ring of the Doughnut model — outlines the maximum sustainable pressure humanity can exert on Earth's life-support systems; exceeding these limits leads to ecosystem overshoot and environmental degradation."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Ecological Ceiling"@en .

thinkr:CrosswalkSource.Wikidata a thinkr:CrosswalkSource,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    skos:prefLabel "Wikidata"@en .

thinkr:ScenarioDimension a thinkr:Category,
        owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "One of the 4 fixed axes in Nate Hagens' 2026 scenario-matrix framework (the 'How to Think About the Future' Frankly series) — Economic, Power & Distribution, Geopolitical, Earth Systems. Each has exactly 4 thinkr:ScenarioFacet options."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Scenario Dimension"@en .

tgs:AlternateTermType.ExactMatch a thinkr:AlternateTermType,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    skos:definition "Genuinely interchangeable terms for the same idea — reusing SKOS's own skos:exactMatch semantics."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Exact Match"@en .

tgs:Concept.DarkTriad a thinkr:Concept,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    thinkr:contrastsWith tgs:Concept.LightTriad ;
    dct:source <https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0191886902001459> ;
    dct:subject tgs:Subject.HumanBehavior ;
    skos:definition "A cluster of three socially aversive personality traits — narcissism, Machiavellianism, and psychopathy — originally proposed by Delroy Paulhus and Kevin Williams (2002). A recurring analytical lens across this graph's source material for understanding how individuals with these traits gain disproportionate influence over institutions and culture, distinct from mere individual pathology."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Dark Triad"@en .

tgs:ResponsePhase.StabilityWindow a thinkr:ResponsePhase,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    skos:definition "The current, finite period in which systems are still connected, real surplus still exists, international coordination is still mostly possible, and institutions — however eroded — are still mostly functioning. Hagens' own real framing: this is the window in which everything that can ONLY be built during stability (institutional trust, physical infrastructure, knowledge transfer, relationships) has to be built, before conditions materially change. The work of this Phase is building and preparing, not yet triaging."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Phase A: The Stability Window"@en .

tgs:ResponsePhase.StableAttractor a thinkr:ResponsePhase,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    skos:definition "NOT a place reached by skipping past Phases A and B — Hagens states this directly, that those periods 'cannot be skipped.' Phase C is instead the destination that gives real meaning and direction to the work of A and B: regenerative, resilient, human-scale, embedded in local ecology, equitable in a way that does not depend on infinite growth to fund redistribution, and rich in meaning and social connection. Hagens' own real framing of who this world is for: the same values that animate opposition to capitalism, ecological destruction, and patriarchy actually have a real home here — not because they were declared into existence, but because the structures that produced their opposite failed and were replaced by something built painstakingly from inside the disruption itself, not after it."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Phase C: The Stable Attractor"@en .

tgs:Persona.GayaHerrington a thinkr:Persona,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    thinkr:actsThrough tgs:Human.GayaHerrington ;
    thinkr:hasAcademicRelationship tgs:Relationship.GayaHerrington_HarvardUniversity ;
    thinkr:hasPersonEntityType thinkr:PersonEntityType.Guest ;
    thinkr:hasProfessionalRelationship tgs:Relationship.GayaHerrington_ClubOfRome,
        tgs:Relationship.GayaHerrington_PostCarbonInstitute,
        tgs:Relationship.GayaHerrington_SchneiderElectric,
        tgs:Relationship.GayaHerrington_StopStraatintimidatie,
        tgs:Relationship.NateHagens_GayaHerrington ;
    skos:prefLabel "Gaya Herrington"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "RETROFITTED 2026-07-15: no Relationship here carries RelationshipType.Personal (all are Professional or Academic), so no hasPersonalRelationship is asserted at all — a real, correct absence, not an oversight, and a genuine test of the new property family (the original filing of all 3 initial Relationships under hasPersonalRelationship was the bug that triggered this whole retrofit). ClubOfRome and PostCarbonInstitute Relationships added same day after a deeper WebFetch of her own bio site surfaced further real, independently-verifiable affiliations beyond the original podcast-intro-driven bootstrap — see humans.ttl for the fuller trail."@en .

thinkr:HagensConcept a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "The narrower subclass of thinkr:Concept specifically for ideas Nate Hagens originated, coined, or gave a genuinely distinctive reframing to himself — as opposed to the broader umbrella, which also covers real ideas/theories he substantively engages with but adopted from elsewhere. ADDED 2026-08-13, raised by MJSullivan specifically to be able to isolate Nate's own unique contributions from the broader set of ideas his show discusses. Classification requires real per-Concept judgment, not a mechanical rule — 'has no documented external lineage yet' is NOT sufficient evidence on its own (several genuinely external ideas, like Terror Management Theory and EROI, had no formal thinkr:influencedBy triple asserted despite being clearly not his own) — each of the 7 initial members was individually checked against its own existing definition/scopeNote before being classified here."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf thinkr:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "Hagens Concept"@en .

tgs:DoughnutHalf.SocialFoundation a thinkr:DoughnutHalf,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dct:source tgs:Work.CaliforniaDoughnutReport2025 ;
    skos:definition "The inner ring of the Doughnut model — tracks the minimum standards of human wellbeing; a shortfall occurs when a metric drops below the threshold necessary for human rights and dignity."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Social Foundation"@en .

tgs:Persona.ArtBerman a thinkr:Persona,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    thinkr:actsThrough tgs:Human.ArtBerman ;
    thinkr:hasPersonEntityType thinkr:PersonEntityType.Guest ;
    thinkr:hasPersonalRelationship tgs:Relationship.NateHagens_ArtBerman ;
    thinkr:hasProfessionalRelationship tgs:Relationship.ArtBerman_TheOilDrum,
        tgs:Relationship.NateHagens_ArtBerman ;
    skos:prefLabel "Art Berman"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "RETROFITTED 2026-07-15: split from a single hasPersonalRelationship list per each Relationship's actual thinkr:hasRelationshipType — see tgs-core.ttl's hasPersonalRelationship comment for the full retrofit story."@en .

tgs:ResponsePhase.BendNotBreak a thinkr:ResponsePhase,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    skos:definition "Already beginning in many places per Hagens' own real framing, and set to arrive with increasing clarity everywhere: financial shocks, supply disruption, social fracture, geopolitical reorganization, and more people falling off the economic treadmill. The work here is fundamentally different from Phase A — largely triage, not building: maintaining critical functions, bridging communities through ruptures, preventing cascades from becoming full collapses, and holding deliberative space open against the real appeal of authoritarian shortcuts. Hagens names the real failure modes of this Phase directly: freezing entirely because the situation is too far outside prior experience, or capitulating to short-term shortcuts and abandoning the long view."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Phase B: Bend Not Break"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Real, direct connection to this graph's own already-built content: the phrase 'Bend Not Break' is Hagens' own long-running term, real source is tgs:Monologue.Frankly_58_FellowshipBendNotBreak ('The Fellowship of the Ring, Bend Not Break Version') — now built as a real Episode individual, resolving what was previously a deferred, not-yet-built reference."@en .

tgs:Subject.Geopolitics a thinkr:Subject,
        owl:NamedIndividual,
        skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme tgs:ConceptScheme.TGSSiteSubjects ;
    skos:prefLabel "Geopolitics"@en .

thinkr:Subject a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "A topic/subject-classification term — NOT the same as thinkr:Concept, which represents a specific idea/claim within a thinker's framework (e.g. 'Overshoot'). Subject is a classification bucket used to organize Concepts and other individuals (e.g. 'Energy Systems'). Explicitly typed both thinkr:Subject AND skos:Concept on every individual, not relying on subclass inference — this project's query tooling doesn't assume a reasoner is running. Used with real SKOS machinery: skos:ConceptScheme, skos:broader, skos:narrower, skos:inScheme, plus the external dct:subject property (not redefined here) to tag other individuals with their relevant Subject(s)."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf skos:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "Subject"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Narrower than skos:Concept: specifically a topic-classification term (see tgs:ConceptScheme.TGSSiteSubjects / MJSullivanDerivedSubtopics), not a TGS framework idea — do not confuse with thinkr:Concept, a different skos:Concept subclass entirely."@en .

tgs:Persona.NoraBateson a thinkr:Persona,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    thinkr:actsThrough tgs:Human.NoraBateson ;
    thinkr:hasPersonalRelationship tgs:Relationship.NateHagens_NoraBateson ;
    thinkr:hasProfessionalRelationship tgs:Relationship.NateHagens_NoraBateson,
        tgs:Relationship.NoraBateson_InternationalBatesonInstitute ;
    skos:prefLabel "Nora Bateson"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Real, extensive prior TGS history confirmed via web search during her original RR-26 bootstrap, deliberately deferred at the time. RESOLVED 2026-08-13, across 3 separate passes: TGS Ep 10, the Frankly episode (Frankly_20, itself a guest-hosted Frankly rather than Nate's usual solo Monologue), Reality Roundtable #10 ('The Ecology of Communication'), and Reality Roundtable #2 ('Deep(er) Ecology,' with William Rees and Rex Weyler) are all now built, sourced from real transcripts + real linked show notes. No further known TGS history remains deferred for Nora as of this note."@en .

thinkr:Category a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "A special class whose instances are enumerated and curated, used to further categorize instances of OTHER classes for more specificity — not a domain entity itself. Formalized 2026-07-11 per MJSullivan's exact definition, marking a pattern that was already implicit in ConfidenceType/ReliabilityType/PolarityType and just-built PersonEntityType. Classes are marked as Category via 'a thinkr:Category' (OWL punning — a class doubling as an instance of this meta-class), not rdfs:subClassOf, since Category-ness is a property of the CLASS itself, not something its own individuals (e.g. ConfidenceType.Curated) inherit. NOTE: thinkr:NamedEntityType is deliberately NOT marked Category — it has zero direct instances of its own (only its subclass PersonEntityType does), so it doesn't meet 'has enumerated curated instances' literally. It's an organizing abstraction, not a Category proper."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Category"@en .

thinkr:ConfidenceType.Candidate a thinkr:ConfidenceType,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    skos:definition "On thinkr:Evidence: LLM-proposed or otherwise unreviewed. On thinkr:LinkNote's calculatedConfidence: no qualifying Curated+Supports evidence exists yet — the default/floor state."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Candidate"@en .

thinkr:NamedEntity a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Superclass for anything that can be surfaced via the NER pipeline (extraction/index_named_entities.py) and formally modeled in the graph. thinkr:Human is currently the only subclass — deliberately left room for others (e.g. an Organization class) to join later without redesigning this. Plain owl:Class, not SKOS — added 2026-07-11 at MJSullivan's direction, correcting an earlier proposal to use SKOS for the same purpose."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Named Entity"@en .

thinkr:Organization a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "A real legal entity — nonprofit, company, community with actual staff/editorial roles — distinct from thinkr:SchoolOfThought (an idea) and thinkr:AcademicInstitution (a university, different relationship verbs apply)."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf thinkr:NamedEntity ;
    skos:prefLabel "Organization"@en .

thinkr:Scenario a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "One specific, named composite future from Nate Hagens' 2026 scenario-matrix framework — a particular combination of exactly one thinkr:ScenarioFacet per thinkr:ScenarioDimension (4 facets total)."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Scenario"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "4 named individuals modeled here, out of 256 mathematically possible combinations (4 Dimensions ^ 4 Facets each) — these 4 are Hagens' own chosen representative examples, not claimed to be exhaustive or equally likely. See scenariofacets.ttl for the 16 individual Facet options this class combines."@en .

tgs:Persona.DanielSchmachtenberger a thinkr:Persona,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    thinkr:actsThrough tgs:Human.DanielSchmachtenberger ;
    thinkr:hasPersonEntityType thinkr:PersonEntityType.Guest ;
    thinkr:hasPersonalRelationship tgs:Relationship.NateHagens_DanielSchmachtenberger ;
    thinkr:hasProfessionalRelationship tgs:Relationship.NateHagens_DanielSchmachtenberger ;
    skos:prefLabel "Daniel Schmachtenberger"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "hasPersonEntityType moved here from tgs:Human.DanielSchmachtenberger, 2026-07-14, Batch 3. hasProfessionalRelationship ADDED 2026-07-15: closing a symmetric-indexing gap found during the has*Relationship audit (see Persona.NateHagens's own scopeNote). hasPersonalRelationship ADDED 2026-08-13, matching the same upgrade on the Relationship itself."@en .

thinkr:PersonalIntervention a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "One of the 15 individual-scale interventions from Frankly_154 — small, specific, real practices Hagens frames as 'seeding' the metacrisis's future starting conditions rather than merely helping a person cope with it. Distinct from thinkr:InterventionSubdomain (societal-scale) and thinkr:Archetype (identity-scale)."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Personal Intervention"@en .

thinkr:SchoolOfThought a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "A philosophical, religious, or intellectual tradition/movement/discipline (e.g. Stoicism, Systems Ecology, Behavioral Economics) — no legal existence, no staff, distinct from thinkr:Organization."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf thinkr:NamedEntity ;
    skos:prefLabel "School of Thought"@en .

thinkr:AlternateTerm a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "A term related to a thinkr:Concept from a different vocabulary, field, or community — may be an anonymous blank node (context-bound, first appearance) or a named individual (promoted once reused across multiple Concepts or once it earns independent citable history of its own)."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Alternate Term"@en .

tgs:EpisodeSegment.Frankly a thinkr:EpisodeSegment,
