    rdfs:subClassOf thinkr:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "Doughnut Indicator"@en .

thinkr:RelationshipType.Personal a thinkr:RelationshipType,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    skos:prefLabel "Personal"@en .

thinkr:CrosswalkNote a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Metadata for a single owl:sameAs crosswalk assertion (which database, when verified, caveats). Same sidecar pattern as thinkr:LinkNote — the actual owl:sameAs triple stays direct and reasoner-compatible, this individual references the same entity+URI pair separately via aboutEntity/aboutExternalURI, rather than reifying owl:sameAs itself."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Crosswalk Note"@en .

tgs:Subject.HumanBehavior a thinkr:Subject,
        owl:NamedIndividual,
        skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme tgs:ConceptScheme.TGSSiteSubjects ;
    skos:prefLabel "Human Behavior"@en .

thinkr:QuadrantNode a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "One of the 49 precomputed lookup points on the real 0-6 grid (7x7), origin (0,0) at the lower-left corner. Each carries its own real hasXPosition/hasYPosition plus precomputed Euclidean distance to each of the 4 real corner positions (QuadrantNode.11/.51/.15/.55), which the 16 real ScenarioFacets are linked to via thinkr:hasQuadrantNode. An arbitrary point (e.g. a classified news article) can be compared to any ScenarioFacet via a direct table lookup rather than live computation."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Quadrant Node"@en .

tgs:Work.CaliforniaDoughnutReport2025 a thinkr:Work,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dct:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode> ;
    dct:source <https://zenodo.org/records/17540639> ;
    rdfs:comment "Authors: Alaitz Aritza (data manager), Julian Kraus-Polk (editor), California Doughnut Economics Coalition. Published November 6, 2025, v1. Examines 42 social/ecological indicators across 21 categories; finds California overshooting 89% of ecological indicators (average overshoot 286%) while falling short on 100% of social indicators assessed. CC-BY 4.0 licensed — more permissive than most sources in this graph, direct quotation with attribution is explicitly permitted."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "The California Doughnut Snapshot and Report"@en .

thinkr:RelationshipType.Professional a thinkr:RelationshipType,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    skos:prefLabel "Professional"@en .

thinkr:Episode a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "A Great Simplification podcast episode or Frankly video."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf thinkr:Work ;
    skos:prefLabel "Podcast Episode"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Narrower than thinkr:Work: specifically a TGS podcast episode or Frankly video, not a book/essay/report."@en .

thinkr:Relationship a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "A stable, self-contained record of a Persona's relationship with another entity — carries hasSubject/hasObject explicitly (not relying on reverse lookup through hasPersonalRelationship), hasRelationshipType (multi-valued), and hasInteraction (nested blank-node instances, solving the multi-instance naming problem). hasSubject/hasObject are Persona, never Human directly — Human is a pure leaf node, reachable only via thinkr:actsThrough."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf thinkr:NamedEntity ;
    skos:prefLabel "Relationship"@en .

thinkr:InteractionRole.Guest a thinkr:InteractionRole,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    skos:prefLabel "Guest"@en .

thinkr:InteractionRole.Host a thinkr:InteractionRole,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    skos:prefLabel "Host"@en .

thinkr:Human a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "A philosopher, scientist, activist, or thinker being linked to a TGS concept."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf thinkr:NamedEntity,
        foaf:Person ;
    skos:prefLabel "Person"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Narrower than foaf:Person: specifically a person being linked to a TGS concept, not any person. Narrower than thinkr:NamedEntity: specifically the subset explicitly typed Person, as distinct from a hypothetical future Organization subclass."@en .

thinkr:PodcastAppearance a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "A single interaction instance within a Relationship — nested as a blank node under hasInteraction, deliberately unnamed (solves the multi-instance naming problem: McGilchrist's 3 separate appearances needed zero additional naming decisions)."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Podcast Appearance"@en .

thinkr:Persona a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "The public-facing identity a Human operates under. Every Relationship, Episode hosting/guesting fact, and (eventually) intellectual-influence claim in this graph belongs to a Persona, not a Human directly — Human holds only biographical facts and is reached solely via thinkr:actsThrough. A new Persona is warranted ONLY when the public name/brand itself genuinely differs from the Human's name (Cher-vs-legal-name level) — not for different professional capacities under one consistent public name, which are multiple thinkr:hasTGSRole values on a single Persona instead."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf thinkr:NamedEntity ;
    skos:prefLabel "Persona"@en .

thinkr:Concept a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "A term or idea discussed within Nate Hagens' Great Simplification framework — the UMBRELLA level, deliberately broad: includes ideas he originated/reframed himself (see the narrower thinkr:HagensConcept subclass) AND real ideas/theories he adopts, synthesizes, or substantively engages with from elsewhere (e.g. Terror Management Theory, Peak Oil, the Superorganism) without having originated them. REVISED 2026-08-13, per MJSullivan's explicit direction, after auditing all 26 existing Concept individuals found the majority (19 of 26) already had documented external origination (15 via explicit thinkr:influencedBy/echoesIdeaOf/contrastsWith links to a real Persona, plus 4 more confirmed external by their own prose) — external adoption/synthesis is the NORM here, not the exception, which is why a narrower subclass for his own originated ideas specifically was worth adding rather than assumed."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf skos:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "Concept"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Narrower than skos:Concept: specifically an idea discussed within Hagens' TGS framework, not a general classification term — do not confuse with thinkr:Subject, which is also a skos:Concept subclass but for topic classification, a different purpose entirely."@en .

